From f0c369534cae24319b419b6e4adf53657ee0269f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: MiaAI-Lab <MiaAI-Lab@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 17:46:28 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] glm: DSpark drafts what a request's tool list forces in a
 tool call (a name's rest, its keys, the tags between; TF_GLM_TOOL_DRAFTS=0:
 off)

Rank 0 reads each request's <tools> block (the first <tools> pair that lists a tool: GLM-5.3's template names the tags
in a sentence first) into the request's copy proposer, the names and parameter keys tokenized as the model writes them
after a tag. DSpark's chain takes the forced token where only one listed name or key continues the call (and the tags
between) and carries on from it; the cursor is built from the stream's context plus the round's kept tokens it does not
hold yet. Drafts only propose: replies stay exact. TP4 K4 (12 parity prompts, 256 tokens): tool tokens a round 2.50 ->
3.04, tool tok/s 30.5 -> 34.8; drafted replies equal the serial ones. TF_GLM_TOOL_DRAFTS_LOG=N logs the first N
cursors. test-glm-tools-host (new); test-glm-dspark-host now runs dspark.zig's tests (the file was not in the module's
test list).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Mythos 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

